/* Deep lessons — Tree algorithms (trees).
 *
 * Trees are usually taught as "graphs, but easier", and that framing loses
 * the whole subject. What makes a tree easy is one fact — between any two
 * nodes there is exactly ONE path — and every technique in this track is a
 * different consequence of it: a subtree is a contiguous range, an ancestor
 * is reachable by powers of two, a path is two half-paths meeting at the LCA,
 * and removing one well-chosen node splits the tree in half.
 *
 * So no stage here starts with code. Each starts with the property it uses,
 * shows the property in a picture, and only then writes the loop.
 *
 * Original text and diagrams. Nothing copied from any source.
 */

import type { DeepLesson } from "../deep-lesson";

